      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the sum of all \\( x \\) that satisfy the equation \\( f^{-1}(x) = f((2x)^{-1}) \\) for the function \\( f(x) = 16x + 3 \\).\n\nFirst, let's find the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\).\n\nGiven \\( f(x) = 16x + 3 \\), we start by setting \\( y = f(x) \\):\n\\[\ny = 16x + 3\n\\]\nSolving for \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\):\n\\[\ny - 3 = 16x\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{y - 3}{16}\n\\]\nThus, the inverse function is:\n\\[\nf^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x - 3}{16}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find \\( f((2x)^{-1}) \\). First, compute \\( (2x)^{-1} \\):\n\\[\n(2x)^{-1} = \\frac{1}{2x}\n\\]\nNow substitute this into \\( f \\):\n\\[\nf\\left( \\frac{1}{2x} \\right) = 16 \\left( \\frac{1}{2x} \\right) + 3 = \\frac{16}{2x} + 3 = \\frac{8}{x} + 3\n\\]\n\nWe are given the equation:\n\\[\nf^{-1}(x) = f((2x)^{-1})\n\\]\nSubstitute the inverse and the function values we found:\n\\[\n\\frac{x - 3}{16} = \\frac{8}{x} + 3\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we first eliminate the fraction by multiplying both sides by \\( 16x \\):\n\\[\nx(x - 3) = 16 \\left( \\frac{8}{x} + 3 \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\nx^2 - 3x = 16 \\left( \\frac{8}{x} + 3 \\right)\n\\]\n\\[\nx^2 - 3x = \\frac{128}{x} + 48\n\\]\n\nNext, multiply through by \\( x \\) to clear the fraction:\n\\[\nx^3 - 3x^2 = 128 + 48x\n\\]\n\\[\nx^3 - 3x^2 - 48x - 128 = 0\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the sum of the roots of the polynomial equation \\( x^3 - 3x^2 - 48x - 128 = 0 \\). By Vieta's formulas, for a cubic equation of the form \\( ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0 \\), the sum of the roots is given by \\( -\\frac{b}{a} \\).\n\nIn our equation, \\( a = 1 \\) and \\( b = -3 \\):\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of the roots} = -\\frac{-3}{1} = 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of all \\( x \\) that satisfy the equation \\( f^{-1}(x) = f((2x)^{-1}) \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
